# Cheat Sheet Authoring

You are editing a board game cheat sheet in `games/`. Follow this schema and style.

## Structure

Use exactly these headings in order (omit empty subsections):

```markdown
# Game Name

## **Setup**
---
### Board setup
...

## **Play**
...

## **Additional details**
...
```

Main sections: bold `##` heading + one `---` line beneath only (no line above).

## Style

- Quick-reference only — terse bullets, imperative voice, no tutorial prose
- **Multi-part steps → sub-bullets** — parent bullet + indented sub-bullets; never chain parts with semicolons on one line
- Official rulebook terminology
- Numbered list for **Step-by-step turn** (one full turn in order)
- **Turn step details** only when a step needs expansion (actions, limits, costs)
- Do not repeat turn summary prose in step details

## Before finishing

- [ ] Setup, Play, and Additional details all present (`## **Title**` + one `---` beneath, no line above)
- [ ] Turn flow is ordered and complete
- [ ] Commonly overlooked rules (if any) after Step-by-step turn, before Turn step details
- [ ] Scoring / end game in Additional details (if applicable)
- [ ] File saved as `games/<lowercase-hyphenated-slug>.md`
- [ ] README [Board Game Index](../../README.md#board-game-index) updated — `- [Game Title](games/<slug>.md)`, alphabetical by title

